# SPEC: 61_memory_management
# static-check: off
# spec/61 §7 regression: `decl v = stringkv.get_copy(k)` (string-valued Kv) must NOT leak per call.
# BUG (fixed 2026-09-25): a string-valued Kv get/get_copy lowers to aiml_db_kv_get (borrow) +
# aiml_str_dup (owned, rc=1), but the dup was NOT registered as an owned string temp. The managed-
# string init-store then treated it as a BORROW and applied an extra aiml_str_incref (rc=2), while
# only ONE scope-drop decref ran → rc stayed 1 → 22 B leaked PER CALL (handle_validate server
# residual ~540 B/req; isolated loop leaked 11,384 B in 501 blocks = 500 per-iteration + 1 open_kv).
# FIX (ast_compiler_call.cpp, string-KV get branch): register the kv_get_own dup on stmtTempStack so
# a consuming decl/set/push/return MOVES it (adopts rc=1, one drop) and a transient is decref'd at
# stmt end. After the fix the isolated loop leaks 0 additional bytes; only the one-time open_kv
# handle (~583 B, a separate Kv-lifetime issue — no `close` yet) remains. This test is FUNCTIONAL
# (corpus): it verifies correctness (total==2600) + no crash across 200 get_copy calls. The leak
# verdict is carried by the isolated valgrind measurement + the mem-sanitizer, not by this file.
- def:
    name: main
    return: i32
    body:
      - decl: [kvs, Kv<string:string>]
      - set: [kvs, { call: [db.open_kv, "skv51", {persist: true, path: "/tmp/skv51_kv/"}] }]
      - call: [kvs.set, "k", "hans@franz.de"]
      - decl: [total, i32, 0]
      - decl: [itr, i32, 0]
      - while:
          condition: { lt: [itr, 200] }
          body:
            - decl: [val, string, { call: [kvs.get_copy, "k"] }]
            - set: [total, { +: [total, val.len] }]
            - set: [itr, { +: [itr, 1] }]
      - if: { condition: { neq: [total, 2600] }, then: [{ print: ["FAIL total=${total} (expected 2600)"] }, { return: 1 }] }
      - print: ["PASS 51 stringkv_getcopy_no_leak"]
      - return: 0
